Feature: Tags
  In the [[v4 rules]], a drone with a [[tagger]] takes enemy drones out of the game. It tags an
  enemy drone that is within 8 m of it, above the trees or over open ground (a lane, a clearing or
  the lake). The tagged drone is down, and its team loses the airframe. Under the trees in the
  forest, a drone cannot be tagged, but nothing can fly there: a low drone is safe only while
  nobody sees it.

  A tagger has two tags. It gets two more at a [[battery swap]]. It counts for nothing in the circle
  of a tower. The enemy sees what kind of drone it is, but not that it carries a tagger until it
  tags.

  Expectation: A tagger tags an enemy drone within 8 m
    Given the tags are on
    And the payload of the first Blue drone is a tagger
    And the tags left of the first Blue drone are 2
    And the first Blue drone is 130 m from the west tower
    And the Red scout is 5 m from the first Blue drone
    When the first Blue drone closes on the Red scout
    Then the condition of the Red scout is down
    And the tags left of the first Blue drone are 1
    And the payload of the first Blue drone on the Red map is a tagger

  Expectation: A drone under the trees cannot be tagged
    Given the tags are on
    And the payload of the first Blue drone is a tagger
    And the tags left of the first Blue drone are 2
    And the first Blue drone is 130 m from the west tower
    And the Red scout is low under the trees, 7 m below the first Blue drone
    When the first Blue drone closes on the Red scout
    Then the condition of the Red scout is flying
    And the tags left of the first Blue drone are 2

  Expectation: A tagger with no tags left tags nothing
    Given the tags are on
    And the payload of the first Blue drone is a tagger
    And the tags left of the first Blue drone are 0
    And the first Blue drone is 130 m from the west tower
    And the Red scout is 5 m from the first Blue drone
    When the first Blue drone closes on the Red scout
    Then the condition of the Red scout is flying
    And the payload of the first Blue drone on the Red map is unknown

  Expectation: A swap gives a tagger two tags
    Given the tags are on
    And the battery swap is on
    And the payload of the first Blue drone is a tagger
    And the tags left of the first Blue drone are 0
    And the first Blue drone is at its base
    When the first Blue drone waits on the ground for its swap
    Then the tags left of the first Blue drone are 2

  Expectation: A tagger counts for nothing in a circle
    Given the tags are on
    And the payload of the first Blue drone is a tagger
    And the west tower is neutral
    And the control of the west tower is 0 %
    And the first Blue drone is in the west circle
    And the Blue drones in the west circle are 1
    When the first Blue drone circles the west tower for 20 seconds
    Then the control of the west tower is 0 %

  Expectation: A tagger that chases uses its battery twice as fast
    A chase is faster than a cruise: more than 20 m/s.

    Given the tags are on
    And the payload of the first Blue drone is a tagger
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 100 s
    And the first Blue drone is 130 m from the west tower
    When the first Blue drone chases for 10 seconds
    Then the battery of the first Blue drone is 80 s
